# MCP Usage

**Mandatory workflow:** [56-dev-mcp-workflow.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/56-dev-mcp-workflow.mdc) — Context7 before code, Supabase for DB, Playwright after UI changes.

Config: workspace `.cursor/mcp.json`; user-global Cursor `mcp.json`.
Never embed API keys in JSON; use `${env:VAR_NAME}`.

Before `call_mcp_tool` / `fetch_mcp_resource`: read tool schema under `mcps/<server>/tools/`.
On failure, record the reason and use a local alternative.

| Task | MCP / skill | Fallback |
|------|-------------|----------|
| Library / API docs (pre-code) | **context7-mcp** / Context7 | Official URL + local `package.json` / `pyproject.toml` |
| DB / schema / SQL | **Supabase MCP** | Local schema files, `pytest` |
| UI / web verification (post-code) | **playwright** skill / Playwright MCP | `npm run test:e2e`, cursor-ide-browser |
| Git history / PR | GitHub MCP, GitLens | `git log`, `gh`, web UI |
| Large design split | Optional | Spec/plan under `docs/superpowers/` |

## Project Rules

- Do not copy external API examples into domain; use application ports and infrastructure adapters.
- Git history inference must be cross-checked against current file contents.
